00:00:04.788 --> 00:00:06.330
GANESH JANAKIRAMAN:
Broadcom Software

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:10.230
is one of the world's leading
enterprise software companies,

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.490
modernizing, optimizing, and
securing some of the world's

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:18.420
largest, most complex
hybrid environments,

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:23.460
and have built a wide portfolio
of industry-leading enterprise

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.440
infrastructure and
security software,

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.340
have the privilege of leading
some of the best engineers

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:33.360
and architects as part of
the SaaS platform engineering

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.720
within Broadcom Software.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.370
We believe that DevOps
is a culture that

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:41.910
fosters innovation, breaks
barriers between development

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.910
and operations teams, improves
efficiencies and productivity.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.320
The primary business
drivers for this effort

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:52.350
was, again, the
diverse portfolio

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.320
of products that
we had within SaaS.

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.890
Broadcom grows organically
and inorganically

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.450
through acquisitions.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:04.319
We acquired products that
are industry leaders, that

00:01:04.319 --> 00:01:06.390
have grown over a
period of time, that

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:08.850
have built on different
technology stacks,

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.590
built with different
methodologies,

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.550
and run on on-prem,
private, and public clouds,

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.150
and operated differently.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:19.860
We had to build a
common standard platform

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:21.840
where these products
could run, where

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.030
we could leverage
the efficiencies

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.650
across these products.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:28.110
This common platform would
include Infrastructure

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:31.260
as a service and the
Kubernetes orchestration layer,

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:35.370
standard DevOps and security
practices adopted across,

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:38.730
and leveraging a common
set of DevSecOps tools,

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.200
like the CI/CD pipeline.

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:44.100
We understood that one
size doesn't fit all.

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.790
But it was surprising,
as we started

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:49.560
migrating many of
these products into

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.150
container-based architectures.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.400
There are a lot
of common strands

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:57.300
across this wide,
heterogeneous set of workloads

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.880
that we had and the
security-- panoply of software

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:00.660
that we had.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.690
We were able to extract a lot
of common strands across, say,

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:08.190
for example, observability, like
monitoring, metrics, alerting,

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.350
logging, and some
of the security

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.580
tooling that we could do that
could monitor this environment.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.340
We were surprised to see the
amount of commonality which

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:20.250
was there that we
could leverage and make

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.170
this whole process
more efficient.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:25.620
Google has been a strong,
reliable partner and a trusted

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:28.180
partner for us in this journey.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.415
And it's fair to say that
without them, we would not

00:02:31.415 --> 00:02:32.790
have been able to
accomplish what

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.010
we did over the last few years.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:39.490
And this is a large program,
a lot of moving parts.

00:02:39.490 --> 00:02:40.680
We did have challenges.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.400
But Google was always
there, available to us,

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.930
responsive, and innovative
in their solutions.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:50.860
Really, this transformation was
not possible without Google.

00:02:50.860 --> 00:02:55.550
And we are definitely
thankful to Google for that.

